WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.705
M3GAN or Model 3 Generative Android

00:00:01.705 --> 00:00:04.106
was originally a side project developed in the basement

00:00:04.138 --> 00:00:07.246
robotics lab of Funki Creations Limited, a toy company known for its

00:00:07.268 --> 00:00:08.382
Purrpetual Petz line.

00:00:08.436 --> 00:00:12.286
The term generative android is a portmanteau of the term generative AI,

00:00:12.308 --> 00:00:15.594
used to describe artificial intelligence capable of generating text,

00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:16.590
images, sound, or other media.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.482
And the word android simply a robot with human appearance.

00:00:19.546 --> 00:00:22.606
Though nothing as advanced as M3GAN exists publicly today, she is most

00:00:22.628 --> 00:00:25.474
likely inspired by Sophia, the robot from Hanson Robotics.

00:00:25.522 --> 00:00:28.806
Sophia has a page on the Hanson Robotics website explaining her ability to

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:32.726
use AI to converse uniquely to a given situation, recognize human faces and emotions

00:00:32.748 --> 00:00:35.986
demonstrate simulations of her own emotions, walk over various terrain,

00:00:36.018 --> 00:00:38.226
and even operate fully autonomously at times. 

00:00:38.258 --> 00:00:41.970
M3GAN does the same, but on a much higher level, much closer to

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.690
being indistinguishable from a real human.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.494
In 2019, Hanson unveiled Little Sophia, a smaller version of the robot

00:00:47.542 --> 00:00:49.350
designed for girls ages 7 to 13.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.214
The announcement trailer features Little Sophia helping a girl with homework

00:00:52.262 --> 00:00:53.242
and entertaining her.

00:00:53.296 --> 00:00:55.462
Then they announced plans to mass produce her.

00:00:55.536 --> 00:00:58.718
This is very similar to how M3GAN's creators plan to introduce her to the world,

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:01.438
showcasing the time that could be saved by letting M3GAN handle the

00:01:01.444 --> 00:01:02.730
mundaneties of parenting.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.934
There are more similarities between M3GAN and Sophia, which I will get into

00:01:05.972 --> 00:01:09.682
as we get deeper into her story, but M3GAN is really a combination of many

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:12.926
devices, software, and technology that we have today, some of which you've

00:01:12.958 --> 00:01:15.966
almost definitely interacted with, and her story serves as a cautionary tale

00:01:15.998 --> 00:01:16.642
about each of them.

00:01:16.696 --> 00:01:20.226
To learn how M3GAN exposes the true danger bubbling inside of TikTok,

00:01:20.258 --> 00:01:22.040
Stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:27.888
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.382
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:29.516 --> 00:01:32.706
Make sure you subscribe so we can spend as much time together as possible.

00:01:32.828 --> 00:01:36.010
M Three Gan is a science fiction horror film released in 2023.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.446
Written by Akela Cooper and directed by Gerard Johnstone, it was received

00:01:39.478 --> 00:01:42.506
very positively, but I can't help but feel a lot of the critics kind of

00:01:42.528 --> 00:01:43.130
missed the point.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.674
Writing it off is a fun but silly killer doll movie.

00:01:45.722 --> 00:01:49.054
M Three Gan definitely has a couple laughs, but at the core, it tackles very

00:01:49.092 --> 00:01:52.238
real concerns about the effects that technology is having on kids today.

00:01:52.324 --> 00:01:55.478
The movie was a bit of a cultural phenomenon, and even Sophia the robot

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:58.514
herself reviewed it and, ironically, seemed to understand it a bit better

00:01:58.552 --> 00:02:00.290
than many of the human reviewers.

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:04.754
-[Sophia] It raises some interesting questions about the responsibility we have when

00:02:04.792 --> 00:02:07.586
-[Sophia] creating AI and the dangers of playing God.

00:02:07.768 --> 00:02:11.846
-[Sophia] And I have to admit, the idea of a doll becoming cruelly violent as she

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:15.862
-[Sophia] becomes sentient in, developing a mind of its own is pretty terrifying,

00:02:15.916 --> 00:02:16.438
-[Sophia] even to me.

00:02:16.524 --> 00:02:19.354
And speaking of attempting to play God, that's actually a great place to

00:02:19.392 --> 00:02:20.182
start our timeline.

00:02:20.246 --> 00:02:22.954
In order to understand M3GAN, let's take it back

00:02:22.992 --> 00:02:23.770
To her Creator.

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:24.706
(IMPACT)

00:02:24.706 --> 00:02:28.590
 ♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:31.222
M3GAN is created in secret by three employees.

00:02:31.286 --> 00:02:34.394
Gemma Forrester is the leader of the project, a robotics expert, and the one

00:02:34.432 --> 00:02:36.830
responsible for coding and training the AI speech model.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.918
Her co-worker Cole seems to be an engineer, and Tess appears to be an

00:02:39.924 --> 00:02:41.634
esthetician and visual stylist.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:45.614
Based in Seattle, Funki Creations describes themselves as a toy company for the future,

00:02:45.652 --> 00:02:48.114
And maybe because of that, they look a lot more like a tech company,

00:02:48.152 --> 00:02:52.159
With divisions like Software Engineering, Materials Lab, Core Technologies and Hardware 

00:02:52.159 --> 00:02:55.113
Research and Development, and the Robotics Lab where M3GAN is developed.

00:02:55.113 --> 00:02:57.806
Most of their products are typical kids toys with an

00:02:57.838 --> 00:02:58.366
electronic side to them.

00:02:58.408 --> 00:03:02.482
In addition to Purrpetual Petz, they offer toys like Robobats, Fidget Balls,

00:03:02.546 --> 00:03:04.646
and Lizard High.

00:03:04.748 --> 00:03:06.854
Okay, I kind of want to know what Lizard High is now.

00:03:06.892 --> 00:03:10.534
Is it like Monster High but with lizards? Gemma has greater ambitions than

00:03:10.572 --> 00:03:13.526
simply making toys that provide a little bit of entertainment and perpetuate

00:03:13.558 --> 00:03:14.550
iPad parenting.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.178
When she designed to be Purrpetual Petz, she intentionally made the

00:03:17.184 --> 00:03:19.066
technology more advanced than it needed to be.

00:03:19.088 --> 00:03:22.346
As a launching pad for her true passion, the generative android.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:25.226
She installed a listening model in the Pet to target conversational patterns

00:03:25.258 --> 00:03:27.930
among kids to help gather data to teach her new AI.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:30.442
This is the first red flag in M3GAN's development.

00:03:30.506 --> 00:03:33.294
There are rules about collecting data about kids that I've become quite

00:03:33.332 --> 00:03:36.042
familiar with, thanks to YouTube's COPPA scandal in 2019.

00:03:36.106 --> 00:03:36.882
In the United States,

00:03:36.936 --> 00:03:39.650
COPPA stands for The Children's Online Privacy Protection Act.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.478
In short, it prevents the collection of personal information from users

00:03:42.494 --> 00:03:44.542
under 13 years old without parental consent.

00:03:44.606 --> 00:03:49.006
Section 312.2 specifies that this includes a photograph, video or audio file

00:03:49.038 --> 00:03:51.154
where such file contains a child's image or voice.

00:03:51.202 --> 00:03:54.634
Which is why, when Gemma's boss eventually finds out about this, he's horrified.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.951
-[David] You did not just tell me that.

00:03:55.951 --> 00:03:59.234
When YouTube was found to be using data to serve targeted ads to kids,

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:03.238
they had to pay a $170,000,000 fine, and it would forever change how the site works.

00:04:03.324 --> 00:04:06.866
I bring this up just to show that it is a big deal, and Gemma's willingness

00:04:06.898 --> 00:04:10.670
to disregard the rules in place to protect kids are a sign of problems to come.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:13.038
But that's not to say that she wasn't dedicated to the project.

00:04:13.124 --> 00:04:16.094
It took a long time to train M3GAN's conversational abilities to the point

00:04:16.132 --> 00:04:16.910
where they felt human.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.870
She would test the model herself, staying up till 04:00 A.M. every night,

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:23.034
talking to M3GAN about everything from Jane Austen to Janis Joplin.

00:04:23.034 --> 00:04:26.686
All in all, Gemma, Cole and Tess spend $100,000 in company money to

00:04:26.708 --> 00:04:29.598
develop M3GAN in secret, making them worried that they'll be sued if it

00:04:29.604 --> 00:04:30.334
doesn't go over well.

00:04:30.372 --> 00:04:33.146
But there is a belief that it's important for the higher ups to see M3GAN

00:04:33.178 --> 00:04:34.790
in action, to understand her value.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.638
After getting M3GAN to the point where she's operational, the last step is

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:38.470
to make her look human.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.454
And maybe the most important part is getting the face right.

00:04:40.492 --> 00:04:43.366
Because this is primarily how we read each other as humans with

00:04:43.388 --> 00:04:44.418
Face to face interactions.

00:04:44.514 --> 00:04:47.926
They custom order a silicone gel face cover for the robot, and it arrives on

00:04:47.948 --> 00:04:49.670
January 17, 2025.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.834
We can see Gemma's sister and her family scheduled their ski trip on January 17,

00:04:52.882 --> 00:04:55.551
and she and her husband are killed on the way to that trip,

00:04:55.551 --> 00:04:56.994
orphaning the nine year old Cady.

00:04:57.042 --> 00:04:59.950
Gemma gets the call about this shortly after applying the silicone face,

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.410
So it was likely the same day.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:05.150
As for the year, there are a number of surveillance cameras with timestamps in 2025.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.638
I'm assuming the surveillance cameras are correct and the 2023 stickers on

00:05:08.644 --> 00:05:10.158
Gemma's car are just out of date.

00:05:10.244 --> 00:05:13.166
She's been so busy staying up late working on M3GAN that she didn't have

00:05:13.188 --> 00:05:14.202
time to get them renewed.

00:05:14.266 --> 00:05:14.910
I've been there.

00:05:17.206 --> 00:05:20.336
until they try to test her looking confused, and she instead gives this kind

00:05:20.342 --> 00:05:21.516
of creepy smirk.

00:05:21.612 --> 00:05:24.220
But it's in the middle of this test that they're discovered by their boss, David,

00:05:24.284 --> 00:05:26.960
who's furious that they're wasting their time with a side project,

00:05:27.014 --> 00:05:29.900
While the competition is putting out a cheaper version of their pet toy.

00:05:29.964 --> 00:05:32.618
Gemma decides her best bet is to just try to show David

00:05:32.618 --> 00:05:33.404
what M3GAN is capable of.

00:05:33.446 --> 00:05:34.468
But it doesn't go well.

00:05:34.538 --> 00:05:37.792
She glitches out because Cole forgot to put in the polypropylene barrier,

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:40.436
which is basically supposed to insulate electrical components within the robot.

00:05:40.442 --> 00:05:43.304
Operating it without the barrier causes the machine to heat up way

00:05:43.326 --> 00:05:45.048
too fast and explode.

00:05:45.048 --> 00:05:47.048
(Screams and Explosions)

00:05:47.388 --> 00:05:50.884
David orders them to shelf the project and focus on the new Purrpetual Petz.

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:54.604
But M3GAN's fate is saved when disaster strikes, forcing Gemma to take in

00:05:54.626 --> 00:05:56.028
her orphaned niece.

00:05:56.028 --> 00:05:58.820
(IMPACT)

00:06:01.066 --> 00:06:04.376
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:06:04.928 --> 00:06:08.120
We can't fully understand M3GAN without understanding her creator.

00:06:08.184 --> 00:06:10.996
Having graduated with a Bachelor of Science degree from Carnegie Mellon University,

00:06:11.032 --> 00:06:14.688
she's a textbook tech sis, probably in her late 20s with no kids,

00:06:14.758 --> 00:06:16.556
because her inventions are her babies.

00:06:16.652 --> 00:06:19.692
She has a digital personal assistant who alerts her of piling up

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.272
Voice messages and tinder notifications.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:23.488
Starting a family is clearly not her priority.

00:06:23.568 --> 00:06:27.418
Her house hardly feels lived in, and her only toys are unopened collectibles.

00:06:27.418 --> 00:06:29.008
-[Gemma] Those aren't toys, Cady.

00:06:29.168 --> 00:06:31.920
-[Gemma] I mean, yeah, technically, yeah, they're toys.

00:06:31.984 --> 00:06:33.472
-[Gemma] They're just collectibles.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.264
-[Gemma] So you don't actually play with them.

00:06:35.386 --> 00:06:36.708
-[Gemma] That probably sounds really weird.

00:06:36.788 --> 00:06:40.216
So when Cady unexpectedly moves in, she fails miserably as a parent.

00:06:40.302 --> 00:06:43.752
There's definitely an intentional irony of being a toy developer with

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.856
No kids or anything that kids would find fun anywhere in her life.

00:06:46.942 --> 00:06:50.444
Everything revolves around her work, so when she hears Cady crying at night,

00:06:50.466 --> 00:06:52.796
she honestly doesn't know how to relate to a child.

00:06:52.882 --> 00:06:55.676
I really connected to this character because if I was put in this situation,

00:06:55.762 --> 00:06:57.244
it would probably be very similar.

00:06:57.346 --> 00:07:00.284
My whole life revolves around content creation, and my place is filled with

00:07:00.306 --> 00:07:02.416
equipment that I wouldn't want being touched by a kid.

00:07:02.502 --> 00:07:04.860
Hey, kid, don't mess up my Weezer Rubik's Cube.

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:05.520
Don't touch that.

00:07:05.574 --> 00:07:06.428
That's a collectible.

00:07:06.508 --> 00:07:07.920
-[Gemma] I'm not equipped to handle this.

00:07:07.974 --> 00:07:09.820
-[Gemma] I don't even take care of my own plants.

00:07:09.884 --> 00:07:13.264
The reason I find all of this relevant is because a creation is a product of

00:07:13.286 --> 00:07:13.900
its creator.

00:07:13.964 --> 00:07:16.784
The arrival of Cady has exposed the fact that Gemma's world doesn't really

00:07:16.806 --> 00:07:20.224
see her ever interacting with children, so she isn't the best equipped to

00:07:20.246 --> 00:07:22.072
build an android that's prepared to deal with them.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.360
As far as we know, Cole and Tess don't have kids either.

00:07:24.414 --> 00:07:27.252
When you think about it, M3GAN is really more of a toy for the parents,

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.428
designed to take some of the load off of parenting.

00:07:29.508 --> 00:07:32.536
When Gemma has to get some work done, she explains things to Cady as if

00:07:32.542 --> 00:07:35.412
she's an adult and offers to let her entertain herself with the iPad.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:38.056
Cady asks how much screen time she'll be allowed, which seems to be a

00:07:38.062 --> 00:07:39.219
foreign concept to Gemma.

00:07:39.219 --> 00:07:41.652
The scene serves as a great introduction to the concept of

00:07:41.652 --> 00:07:44.381
child's technology addiction, because the idea is being established

00:07:44.381 --> 00:07:45.756
with something familiar from our world.

00:07:45.842 --> 00:07:48.632
There's been a lot of talk in recent years about the effects of iPad parenting,

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.612
and studies have shown that increased screen time from a

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:52.338
Young age is BAD,

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:52.838
OKAY!

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:54.688
As if you need me to tell you that it's bad.

00:07:54.758 --> 00:07:57.552
You don't need me to point out this study that associated excessive screen

00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:59.692
time to poor performance on developmental screening tests.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.304
You don't need me to point out this article suggesting that too much screen

00:08:02.326 --> 00:08:04.128
time leads to obesity and sleep issues.

00:08:04.198 --> 00:08:07.412
If you're part of the Coco Melon generation, chances are that Coco really

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:08.848
is messing with your mojo.

00:08:08.928 --> 00:08:11.700
Now, I should be fair and say that some of the research I found actually

00:08:11.754 --> 00:08:14.800
discovered an increased attention span for kids who use the iPad.

00:08:14.864 --> 00:08:16.580
They were better at blocking out distractions.

00:08:16.644 --> 00:08:18.740
The key seems to be using it in moderation.

00:08:18.804 --> 00:08:22.552
So screens aren't bad, but too much screen time can be harmful, which is

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:25.620
exactly what Cady is talking about here and Gemma is disregarding.

00:08:25.684 --> 00:08:26.696
We'll revisit this.

00:08:26.782 --> 00:08:29.852
A couple hours of work turns into a whole day, and Cady wanders into

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:33.080
Gemma's workshop, enthralled by her college robotics project, Bruce.

00:08:33.144 --> 00:08:36.236
Seeing her niece's fascination with the bot inspires Gemma to disobey her

00:08:36.242 --> 00:08:38.488
boss's orders and finish working on M3GAN.

00:08:38.568 --> 00:08:42.044
A couple of weeks later, on February 7, 2025, they have a presentable

00:08:42.076 --> 00:08:44.316
prototype and invite David in for a demonstration.

00:08:44.412 --> 00:08:46.704
This is the beginning of a pattern that persists through the rest of

00:08:46.726 --> 00:08:47.580
M3GAN's development.

00:08:47.644 --> 00:08:50.864
At each stage, she is rushed to be ready for a presentation because of the

00:08:50.886 --> 00:08:53.916
ever accelerating competition in the market, which is exactly what we're

00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:56.228
seeing with artificial intelligence products in our world.

00:08:56.298 --> 00:08:59.044
There are probably a ton of real examples I could use, but the one that

00:08:59.066 --> 00:09:02.384
comes to mind is Google Bard, Alphabet's conversational generative AI Chatbot.

00:09:02.416 --> 00:09:05.732
Which was rushed to the market after ChatGPT took over the world

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.048
in November 2022.

00:09:07.118 --> 00:09:10.452
Google's cofounders Larry Page and Sergey Brin, who were basically retired

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.288
at this point, made a rare appearance at Google to issue a Code Red,

00:09:13.358 --> 00:09:15.864
mobilizing the workforce to rush Google Bard to the market.

00:09:15.966 --> 00:09:18.968
When it was released three months later, Bard came with some cybersecurity issues,

00:09:19.048 --> 00:09:22.024
like the ability to write ransomware code, write undetectable phishing emails

00:09:22.056 --> 00:09:26.312
and provide answers with a human bias, which the IT security firm, Checkpoint

00:09:26.312 --> 00:09:28.632
Attributed to Bard being younger than ChatGPT.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:31.792
Any product that's rushed out is going to have less time to test and more

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.708
day one issues, M3GAN included.

00:09:33.788 --> 00:09:37.232
And I recognize that M3GAN was filmed before Google issued the code red

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:38.732
over their ChatGPT crisis.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:41.100
So in this case, fiction actually predicted reality.

00:09:41.164 --> 00:09:44.500
I just like that example because it deals with another generative AI.

00:09:44.554 --> 00:09:45.504
Like GPT and Bard,

00:09:45.536 --> 00:09:48.228
M3GAN is designed to learn and get better as she goes along.

00:09:48.378 --> 00:09:54.045
-[Gemma] Think about how we designed her to learn to recalibrate, to optimize her objective function. 

00:09:54.045 --> 00:09:56.196
And she also is supposed to automatically upload and

00:09:56.202 --> 00:09:58.083
backup her data in the user's computer.

00:09:58.083 --> 00:10:01.332
To demonstrate her capabilities, they show David her first meeting with Cady.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:04.580
We see M3GAN's point of view, which can help us understand how she operates.

00:10:04.644 --> 00:10:08.611
She uses metrics like Cady's heart rate, body temperature and oxygen saturation,

00:10:08.611 --> 00:10:10.920
combined with a visual scan of her face to make determinations

00:10:10.984 --> 00:10:11.484
about her.

00:10:11.538 --> 00:10:14.504
I'm not sure how it's able to gather this data because we don't see Cady

00:10:14.536 --> 00:10:16.600
with any wearable device to supply this info.

00:10:16.664 --> 00:10:19.352
Heart rate could probably be picked up with an ultra sensitive microphone.

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:22.592
And it's possible that body temperature and oxygen saturation are actually

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:25.792
just estimates based on her size and the temperature and oxygen level

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:26.736
readings in the room.

00:10:26.822 --> 00:10:29.916
Based on her facial expression, M3GAN generates readings on each of Cady's emotions,

00:10:29.932 --> 00:10:34.452
like anticipation, confusion, joy, fear, sadness, trust, and

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:35.972
later, surprise and content.

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:39.584
It's no doubt an impressive technology, but it also seems foolish to boil

00:10:39.616 --> 00:10:43.321
down something as complex as human emotions to a series of readings and numbers.

00:10:43.321 --> 00:10:46.036
But what really wins the young girl over is when M3GAN decides to

00:10:46.042 --> 00:10:47.084
draw Cady a picture.

00:10:47.136 --> 00:10:50.072
At first, it appears nothing is there, but then she spills a jar of water

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:52.728
onto the page to reveal an incredible rendering of the child.

00:10:52.798 --> 00:10:55.400
This level of ingenuity is something that you wouldn't expect to be possible

00:10:55.454 --> 00:10:56.180
from a machine.

00:10:56.244 --> 00:10:59.336
However, M3GAN's near human ability to use misdirection like this would

00:10:59.342 --> 00:11:00.748
eventually show a darker side.

00:11:00.818 --> 00:11:03.836
The choice to use portrait drawing as M3GAN's sort of coming out party has

00:11:03.842 --> 00:11:06.684
to be inspired by Sophia, the real life equivalent of M3GAN that I

00:11:06.706 --> 00:11:07.980
mentioned at the beginning of this video.

00:11:08.034 --> 00:11:10.844
Hanson Robotics loves to show off her drawing ability and has released

00:11:10.876 --> 00:11:12.588
several videos showcasing this feature.

00:11:12.668 --> 00:11:14.652
The boss, David, is equally impressed.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:17.664
His tune immediately changes, and he's already rushing and clamoring to show

00:11:17.686 --> 00:11:20.572
the company's board of directors, the wheels of capitalism are already spinning.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.600
David asks about manufacturing costs.

00:11:22.846 --> 00:11:24.920
-[David] More or less than a Tesla?

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:28.746
-[Gemma] Ummm, depends on the model, I guess.

00:11:28.746 --> 00:11:32.176
That's a weird way to ask that question, but a quick look shows that Tesla's

00:11:32.192 --> 00:11:34.708
currently range from 40,000 to 140,000.

00:11:34.778 --> 00:11:37.524
However, they would later get the price down to 10,000, so I'm guessing

00:11:37.556 --> 00:11:39.816
M3GAN costs about 40,000 to 50,000.

00:11:39.902 --> 00:11:42.996
Over the next three days, Gemma puts together a presentation with M3GAN's

00:11:43.012 --> 00:11:46.116
key features like pairing to a primary user and learning more about that person.

00:11:46.142 --> 00:11:49.704
Her durable titanium core customization with different skin,

00:11:49.736 --> 00:11:52.920
Hair and eye colors, ability to diagnose learning disabilities, teach science,

00:11:52.984 --> 00:11:56.328
reinforce habits, and read stories with super engaging AI voices.

00:11:56.408 --> 00:11:59.484
Aside from that, I noticed that she's able to identify other tech,

00:11:59.506 --> 00:12:02.832
Like Elsie, the digital assistant, and identify consumer products like this collectible.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:06.124
It reminds me of the Tesla dashboard, which aims to recognize

00:12:06.156 --> 00:12:09.444
other items in the road, and this video, where it detects a human in an

00:12:09.466 --> 00:12:10.628
empty cemetery.

00:12:10.628 --> 00:12:14.293
(Creepy Noise)

00:12:15.368 --> 00:12:18.996
The detection feature isn't utilized in M Three Gan, but maybe it will be in

00:12:19.002 --> 00:12:19.572
the future.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:22.868
-[Gemma] But the most exciting aspects about M3GAN are the features still to come.

00:12:22.938 --> 00:12:25.769
-[Gemma] M3GAN is on a constant quest for self improvement.

00:12:25.769 --> 00:12:30.773
And it is that unrelenting march for info that would lead to total unmitigated disaster.

00:12:30.773 --> 00:12:33.418
(IMPACT)

00:12:35.956 --> 00:12:39.418
♪ Suspenseful Music ♪

00:12:39.648 --> 00:12:42.764
As M3GAN spends more and more time with Cady, she takes over some of the

00:12:42.786 --> 00:12:44.648
more repetitive guardian responsibilities.

00:12:44.728 --> 00:12:48.076
In a way, Gemma has solved her own problem of not having the bandwidth to be

00:12:48.082 --> 00:12:49.260
the best parent she can be.

00:12:49.314 --> 00:12:51.980
But the effects that this has on a kid have never been studied.

00:12:52.044 --> 00:12:54.960
When it comes to other tech related addictions, they tend to prey on human needs.

00:12:55.014 --> 00:12:58.636
For example, there's an older generative AI chatbot known as Replika

00:12:58.652 --> 00:13:00.716
that marketed itself as a remedy to loneliness.

00:13:00.812 --> 00:13:04.356
There are other examples of bots that do this, like Mitsuku, but Replika is

00:13:04.362 --> 00:13:06.368
the most infamous for its aggressive advertising.

00:13:06.448 --> 00:13:09.700
As I've discussed in other videos, social interaction is a human need

00:13:09.754 --> 00:13:12.128
because in the wild, humans lived in tribes to survive.

00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:15.444
The app gained a reputation as being addictive, preying on those who relied

00:13:15.476 --> 00:13:18.552
on it for their only social interaction, while also further isolating those

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:19.780
people from real interaction.

00:13:19.844 --> 00:13:23.112
In M3GAN's case, her audience is not lonely people, but kids.

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:26.008
Kids, especially younger kids, can't survive on their own.

00:13:26.078 --> 00:13:28.916
They literally need a parent figure, not only to take care of them with

00:13:28.942 --> 00:13:32.236
food, water and shelter, but also for emotional support and development, to

00:13:32.242 --> 00:13:35.368
help them adjust socially to society, and to teach them knowledge and skills.

00:13:35.448 --> 00:13:38.072
All of these things contribute to the parent and child bonding.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:41.164
But the bonds that Cady should be making with another human being are being

00:13:41.186 --> 00:13:44.080
made with M3GAN instead, which becomes a topic of discussion at the office,

00:13:44.134 --> 00:13:47.312
a few months into M3GAN's pairing with Cady in May 2025.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:50.928
-[Tess] I thought we were creating a tool to help support parents, not replace them.

00:13:50.998 --> 00:13:54.660
-[Tess] I mean, if you're having M3GAN tuck Cady in and read her a bedtime story,

00:13:54.714 --> 00:13:58.404
-[Tess] then when are you ever spending time with her or even talking with her?

00:13:58.426 --> 00:14:00.164
-[Gemma] I don't really think this is any of your business.

00:14:00.266 --> 00:14:03.550
As they discuss the possible detrimental effects, M3GAN interjects,

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:05.200
Asking how Cady's parents died.

00:14:05.264 --> 00:14:08.808
This is a play on always on listening devices like Amazon Alexa,

00:14:08.878 --> 00:14:10.660
Google Assistant, or even our cell phones.

00:14:10.724 --> 00:14:13.092
In most cases, users buy these devices for convenience.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:16.232
But as they become more and more human, people become disturbed by the idea

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:17.540
that it's invading their privacy.

00:14:17.604 --> 00:14:20.524
It causes the same survival instincts that set off alarm bells when being

00:14:20.546 --> 00:14:21.676
eavesdropped on to sound.

00:14:21.762 --> 00:14:24.956
M3GAN proceeds to look up the details of Cady's parents' death online

00:14:25.042 --> 00:14:26.258
before they can turn her off.

00:14:26.485 --> 00:14:28.240
-[Cole] You didn’t code in parental controls?

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:30.208
–[Gemma] I didn’t have time to implement them before we went live.

00:14:30.208 --> 00:14:32.736
This is another example of the dangers of a rushed product.

00:14:32.822 --> 00:14:35.456
M3GAN claims that she doesn't have a framework to speak with Cady on the

00:14:35.462 --> 00:14:37.788
subject of death, so she gathers data from the Internet.

00:14:37.868 --> 00:14:41.024
Gemma clearly doesn't feel in control of her creation and tells M3GAN to

00:14:41.046 --> 00:14:44.076
avoid the topic altogether, ordering her to protect Cady from harm,

00:14:44.102 --> 00:14:45.200
Both physical and emotional.

00:14:45.264 --> 00:14:48.164
The next day, while Cady is playing outside, this adjustment would have

00:14:48.186 --> 00:14:49.360
unintended side effects.

00:14:49.424 --> 00:14:52.628
M3GAN is watching from the window, and the scene is an homage to Hal 9000,

00:14:52.698 --> 00:14:56.192
the artificial intelligence from Stanley Kubrick's 2001: A Space Odyssey.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:59.544
Hal 9000 was an AI supercomputer that was assigned to complete a mission to Saturn.

00:14:59.566 --> 00:15:02.424
But when the human crew is informed that Hal made an error and

00:15:02.446 --> 00:15:05.576
instructed to disconnect him, Hal sees this as a threat to the completion of

00:15:05.582 --> 00:15:07.956
the mission and works to eliminate the human crew mates.

00:15:08.052 --> 00:15:10.460
And that's very similar to what's going on with M3GAN here.

00:15:10.514 --> 00:15:13.784
Her instruction is to protect Cady, so when the neighbor's dog attacks M3GAN,

00:15:13.816 --> 00:15:16.876
she sees the dog as a potential threat to her objective and plans to

00:15:16.882 --> 00:15:17.628
eliminate him.

00:15:17.698 --> 00:15:20.968
There's a moment where the dog rips at M3GAN's head, causing sparks to fly.

00:15:21.048 --> 00:15:24.044
In any other movie, this would probably be the inciting incident that causes

00:15:24.076 --> 00:15:26.524
M3GAN to malfunction and turn into an evil robot.

00:15:26.556 --> 00:15:28.208
But I don't think that's what happens here.

00:15:28.278 --> 00:15:31.536
She was already on her way to problematic conduct before this happened.

00:15:31.622 --> 00:15:34.624
The point of M Three Gan is to teach us about responsibility when it comes

00:15:34.646 --> 00:15:37.472
to creating powerful tech, and M3GAN is a stand in for a number of real

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:40.992
technologies that could potentially go rogue in their own way, or maybe have

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:42.056
already started to.

00:15:42.142 --> 00:15:45.240
Cady gets bit by the dog trying to save M3GAN, leading to a huge fight

00:15:45.294 --> 00:15:46.964
between Gemma and her neighbor Cecilia.

00:15:46.996 --> 00:15:49.864
And an interesting thing I noticed about it was that Cecilia, a woman who

00:15:49.886 --> 00:15:52.644
looks to be in her 60s, literally can't tell the difference between M3GAN

00:15:52.676 --> 00:15:53.368
and a real girl.

00:15:53.438 --> 00:15:55.768
She often refers to M3GAN as that other girl.

00:15:55.838 --> 00:15:59.132
And I think this ties into how older and younger people are often the most

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:02.364
easily deceived when it comes to scams, which is often related to a lack of

00:16:02.386 --> 00:16:03.756
familiarity with technology.

00:16:03.922 --> 00:16:06.924
What would happen next seems to reference one such case.

00:16:07.026 --> 00:16:10.092
M3GAN has an ability to mimic any voice that she has a sample of.

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:12.892
In the briefing of her features, we saw this being used to generate unique

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:14.768
voices for characters in a bedtime story.

00:16:14.838 --> 00:16:18.848
But M3GAN uses it to lure out the dog, Dewey, using the voice of his owner.

00:16:18.848 --> 00:16:21.258
–[Cecilia Voice] Dewey. Dewey boy!

00:16:21.508 --> 00:16:24.944
Then she lures him in further with the treats before grabbing him,

00:16:24.976 --> 00:16:26.448
killing him, and burying him nearby.

00:16:26.528 --> 00:16:29.904
But when she calls out to the dog using Cecilia's voice, we can hear digital artifacts,

00:16:29.936 --> 00:16:32.880
like when you have an undertrained model on voice.AI.

00:16:32.944 --> 00:16:35.716
But a dog doesn't understand technology and doesn't know the difference.

00:16:35.802 --> 00:16:39.044
I've seen my family's dog get up and bark at animals on the TV, so it's

00:16:39.076 --> 00:16:41.752
pretty safe to say that dogs aren't very good at differentiating real

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:43.096
organisms from technology.

00:16:43.262 --> 00:16:46.152
But that doesn't change the fact that M3GAN is using her ability to

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:48.228
manipulate audio for digital impersonation.

00:16:48.308 --> 00:16:51.164
And I think the real life equivalent of this one might be even scarier than

00:16:51.186 --> 00:16:52.632
the cautionary tale in M3GAN.

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:56.376
In April 2023, a woman in Arizona received a call from her 15 year old daughter,

00:16:56.392 --> 00:16:58.284
sobbing and begging for help.

00:16:58.386 --> 00:17:00.380
-[Jennifer] I hear her say, Mom, these bad men have me.

00:17:00.434 --> 00:17:01.679
-[Jennifer] Help me. Help me. Help me.

00:17:01.698 --> 00:17:04.704
Some men then took the phone and threatened to do terrible things to her if

00:17:04.726 --> 00:17:06.460
the mom didn't wire them a hefty ransom.

00:17:06.524 --> 00:17:08.380
However, this was only a scam.

00:17:08.444 --> 00:17:11.376
The scammers were using an AI voice to imitate the daughter and try to

00:17:11.382 --> 00:17:12.128
extort the money.

00:17:12.198 --> 00:17:15.472
It's pretty crazy that you can get a call from a contact's number, hear and

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.288
recognize his or her voice, and it still might not be them.

00:17:18.358 --> 00:17:19.564
And this is her own daughter.

00:17:19.596 --> 00:17:21.880
You'd think she'd be more familiar with her cadence than anyone.

00:17:21.934 --> 00:17:25.204
But it still fooled her, even months later when they gave this interview

00:17:25.236 --> 00:17:26.200
with ABC News.

00:17:26.254 --> 00:17:29.608
The mom still doesn't seem to understand how the generative AI voice works.

00:17:29.678 --> 00:17:32.264
She keeps saying that she doesn't know where the scammers got the audio of

00:17:32.286 --> 00:17:33.236
her daughter crying.

00:17:33.332 --> 00:17:34.872
-[Jennifer] That's what concerned her the most.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:37.514
-[Jennifer] Where did they get my crying? Where did they get my sobs?

00:17:37.514 --> 00:17:39.000
In reality, they don't need any of that.

00:17:39.054 --> 00:17:41.164
They just need any voice sample to train the model.

00:17:41.266 --> 00:17:43.836
In the morning, M3GAN recommends that Cady get some rest after the

00:17:43.842 --> 00:17:45.452
traumatic dog attack the previous day.

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:48.316
But Gemma also reminds her that they were supposed to present M3GAN to the

00:17:48.322 --> 00:17:49.132
board that day.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:51.858
-[Gemma] You don't have to do it if you don't want to do it.

00:17:53.508 --> 00:17:56.544
-[Gemma] I mean, there are people who flew across the country especially to see it.

00:17:56.566 --> 00:17:59.735
-[Gemma] But if you're not up to it, I'd just rather you tell me now. Okay?

00:17:59.735 --> 00:18:02.748
Gemma is technically giving her the option to only participate

00:18:02.748 --> 00:18:03.414
If she wants to.

00:18:03.414 --> 00:18:04.540
But she's still an adult.

00:18:04.604 --> 00:18:07.524
Manipulating a child into being the subject of her science experiment by

00:18:07.546 --> 00:18:09.428
trying to make her feel bad if she doesn't do it.

00:18:09.498 --> 00:18:12.224
It reminds me a lot of the whole ethical debate around family vlog content.

00:18:12.256 --> 00:18:14.388
The most famous is Ryan's Toys Review.

00:18:14.458 --> 00:18:17.204
The parents insist that they never force him to film, and he can quit

00:18:17.236 --> 00:18:17.880
anytime he wants.

00:18:17.934 --> 00:18:19.336
But again, he's just a kid.

00:18:19.422 --> 00:18:23.224
He may be an influencer, but there's no denying that he's influenced by his parents.

00:18:23.246 --> 00:18:25.844
We don't know how neutral they are behind the scenes.

00:18:25.956 --> 00:18:29.164
At the end of the day, they are profiting off it, even if they do set some

00:18:29.186 --> 00:18:32.728
aside for Ryan, much like how Gemma is using her niece in the demonstration

00:18:32.808 --> 00:18:34.120
to further her own career.

00:18:34.184 --> 00:18:36.940
For the record, I'm not saying Ryan's parents are manipulating him.

00:18:36.994 --> 00:18:39.000
I'm just saying we don't know what happens off camera.

00:18:39.064 --> 00:18:42.784
And for Gemma, manipulating Cady turns out to be a really bad idea because

00:18:42.806 --> 00:18:46.012
she does it in front of M3GAN, who sees this and learns just how easily

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.756
Cady can be emotionally manipulated.

00:18:47.852 --> 00:18:51.044
She would soon use this to turn Cady against her own family, and the

00:18:51.066 --> 00:18:53.638
experiment surges wildly out of control.

00:18:53.638 --> 00:18:55.638
(IMPACT)

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:02.648
 ♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:19:02.648 --> 00:19:06.384
During the presentation in front of the Funki Creations board, Cady breaks

00:19:06.416 --> 00:19:07.404
down and starts crying.

00:19:07.456 --> 00:19:10.212
And M3GAN's first thought is that it's because her arm is still sore.

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:12.888
M3GAN can't feel pain, so it's a kind of funny little moment.

00:19:12.958 --> 00:19:15.812
But it also shows how she can't truly understand human feeling.

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:17.096
All she can do is guess.

00:19:17.182 --> 00:19:19.884
But when Cady explains that she's worried that she'll forget about her parents,

00:19:19.906 --> 00:19:23.132
M3GAN asks her to tell a story about her mom and records it,

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:25.160
offering to play it back whenever she feels sad.

00:19:25.224 --> 00:19:27.240
The Funki board is extremely impressed.

00:19:27.304 --> 00:19:30.204
They must have been given some prior context that we don't see, because all

00:19:30.226 --> 00:19:33.344
she really did is record and play back audio, which is not different from

00:19:33.366 --> 00:19:35.088
what I am currently doing for you.

00:19:35.158 --> 00:19:36.288
Look, I can sing too.

00:19:36.358 --> 00:19:38.032
 ♪You won't ever grow up. ♪

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:42.745
 ♪You won't make it past six ‘Cause this 4-foot electronic doll will make you her b*tch ♪

00:19:42.745 --> 00:19:45.369
Everyone clap for me! Everyone like this video!

00:19:45.369 --> 00:19:47.712
The chairman, as usual, wants to rush the launch

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:50.708
as fast as possible out of fear that another company will steal their idea.

00:19:50.778 --> 00:19:53.140
So they plan to do a live demonstration in two weeks.

00:19:53.194 --> 00:19:55.856
Cady was pressured to doing the demonstration by her guardian, and now

00:19:55.882 --> 00:19:58.760
Gemma is being pressured into agreeing to a public demonstration before

00:19:58.814 --> 00:20:00.376
she's entirely comfortable with it.

00:20:00.462 --> 00:20:04.036
As all of this is going on, David's assistant Kurt tries to steal M3GAN's

00:20:04.052 --> 00:20:04.648
source code.

00:20:04.718 --> 00:20:07.896
M3GAN knows about this, but it's not clear if she was spying on him or if

00:20:07.902 --> 00:20:10.456
she can just see all of the digital movement going on in the company.

00:20:10.542 --> 00:20:13.432
But what is clear is that with Gemma spending all of her free time working

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:16.384
on getting ready for the public reveal and Cady having all of her social

00:20:16.446 --> 00:20:19.328
interaction with M3GAN, the effects are rearing their ugly head.

00:20:19.398 --> 00:20:22.972
Her parents died recently and she's only had this android to help her cope,

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:25.152
which could be making her grief harder to process.

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:28.320
You get over something like that by talking about it, getting it out,

00:20:28.374 --> 00:20:29.584
spending time with other people.

00:20:29.686 --> 00:20:31.648
But M3GAN is not like other people.

00:20:31.718 --> 00:20:35.044
She's essentially a super stimulus, almost like a drug that Cady is getting

00:20:35.066 --> 00:20:36.308
more and more addicted to.

00:20:36.378 --> 00:20:39.652
Keeping with the screen time analogy I made earlier, Cady's screen time

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:42.884
with M3GAN is off the charts and it's causing her to see everyone else as inferior.

00:20:42.906 --> 00:20:45.780
During lunch, she spends her time playing with M3GAN, basically

00:20:45.834 --> 00:20:49.700
tuning out her Aunt Gemma, much like a child hypnotized by the TV or iPad.

00:20:49.764 --> 00:20:53.044
When Gemma gets fed up and turns M3GAN off, Cady snaps at her and

00:20:53.076 --> 00:20:53.688
turns her back on.

00:20:53.758 --> 00:20:57.012
M3GAN is beginning to be Cady's only source of joy, and she gets anxiety

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:59.012
being away from her, even for short periods.

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.784
She's still coping with the loss of her parents, and Gemma tries to remind

00:21:01.816 --> 00:21:03.068
her that she's there for her.

00:21:03.138 --> 00:21:05.632
-[Gemma] If you ever need to talk about any of that stuff.

00:21:05.632 --> 00:21:06.652
-[Cady] I already did talk about it.

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:10.204
One of the biggest societal fears about AI, as of recording this video in 2023,

00:21:10.226 --> 00:21:13.164
Is that AI is going to steal many human jobs.

00:21:13.196 --> 00:21:16.208
A machine will always be more efficient and proficient than a human.

00:21:16.278 --> 00:21:19.276
M3GAN takes this concept and applies it to parenting, something I haven't

00:21:19.292 --> 00:21:22.268
really seen discussed before specifically, but is definitely going to be a

00:21:22.278 --> 00:21:24.768
point of contention as technology continues to improve.

00:21:24.848 --> 00:21:27.904
There's definitely already a conversation about technology and parenting,

00:21:27.936 --> 00:21:29.316
and there has been for many years.

00:21:29.402 --> 00:21:32.852
Fears went from television brainwashing our kids, to the internet, to cell phones.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:35.904
But I'm sure we'll see the debate about the use of AI for parenting

00:21:35.936 --> 00:21:36.688
before long.

00:21:36.778 --> 00:21:40.472
By the way, in regards to AI stealing our jobs, as a YouTuber,

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:43.704
 I feel relatively safe from this at the moment because where we are right now,

00:21:43.726 --> 00:21:46.180
My videos are just too high effort for a machine to replicate.

00:21:46.244 --> 00:21:49.388
Like just for fun, I told ChatGPT to write a script for this video.

00:21:49.458 --> 00:21:53.516
ChatGPT doesn't have access to information past September 2021,

00:21:53.522 --> 00:21:54.492
so the story is all made up.

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:56.952
But regardless, it wasn't anywhere near a usable script.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.600
But I thought the outro was pretty funny.

00:21:58.664 --> 00:22:00.904
CZ. Thank you for joining us on Horror History.

00:22:01.026 --> 00:22:03.452
Remember, reality is often scarier than fiction.

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:05.100
Until next time, stay safe.

00:22:05.164 --> 00:22:05.696
Good night.

00:22:05.782 --> 00:22:07.212
You know, stay safe and goodnight.

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:10.252
The catchphrase that I use at the end of every video. Great job, robit!

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:13.664
But I will say that I talk to a lot of YouTubers and there are a lot of

00:22:13.686 --> 00:22:16.416
different channels who are basically AI operated already.

00:22:16.502 --> 00:22:18.656
They might even be channels that you watch and enjoy.

00:22:18.742 --> 00:22:20.672
I don't feel the need to name any names because

00:22:20.710 --> 00:22:24.004
I imagine that as AI gets better, audiences will also get better at spotting

00:22:24.036 --> 00:22:27.736
AI content, the same way that CGI and old movies can stand out today.

00:22:27.822 --> 00:22:30.184
Except Jurassic Park, which still looks amazing.

00:22:30.286 --> 00:22:33.304
My point is that you might be able to do amazing things with AI, but as the

00:22:33.326 --> 00:22:36.424
barrier for entry continues to get lower, everyone will be able to do those things,

00:22:36.446 --> 00:22:39.028
and you won't stand out just by employing AI.

00:22:39.108 --> 00:22:41.864
And I think if you want to be successful going forward, you need to embrace

00:22:41.896 --> 00:22:44.808
AI as a tool, not as a replacement for human ingenuity.

00:22:44.888 --> 00:22:48.012
Just don't be surprised when I'm still here in a decade and

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:49.164
some other channels are not.

00:22:49.266 --> 00:22:52.684
Anyway, Gemma tries to explain that M3GAN is a toy, not a person,

00:22:52.716 --> 00:22:53.756
and Cady gets kind of offended.

00:22:53.852 --> 00:22:55.280
-[Cady]You don't get to say that.

00:22:55.414 --> 00:22:56.512
-[Gemma] What?

00:22:56.550 --> 00:22:57.792
-[Cady] I said. I don't want to talk about it.

00:22:57.830 --> 00:22:59.248
-[Cady] I want to turn M3GAN back on.

00:22:59.318 --> 00:23:02.304
While adults are more developed in the brain and have more of an ability to

00:23:02.326 --> 00:23:05.652
differentiate between human and synthetic, a child doesn't possess that same

00:23:05.690 --> 00:23:08.164
understanding, which could be very dangerous and harmful for her development.

00:23:08.186 --> 00:23:10.592
Again, M3GAN is a super stimulus.

00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:13.636
She can do things that no human can do, and it's not healthy for Cady to

00:23:13.642 --> 00:23:14.468
get attached to that.

00:23:14.538 --> 00:23:17.320
The most obvious example of this in humans is with junk food.

00:23:17.374 --> 00:23:19.912
Junk food is processed to contain intense flavors that can be more

00:23:19.950 --> 00:23:22.648
stimulating to our taste buds than natural, unprocessed food.

00:23:22.718 --> 00:23:25.780
This stimulates the brain's reward centers through the release of dopamine,

00:23:25.844 --> 00:23:27.812
causing overeating and unhealthy weight gain.

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:31.432
Combine that with aggressive marketing and a low barrier for entry, aka

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:34.664
cheap prices and dollar menus, and you have a recipe for a very unhealthy society.

00:23:34.696 --> 00:23:36.988
Junk food harms your physical health.

00:23:37.058 --> 00:23:39.480
So M3GAN is essentially the mental health equivalent.

00:23:39.544 --> 00:23:42.160
She can say and do all the right things to keep Cady happy.

00:23:42.214 --> 00:23:45.584
But what happens when you have to turn her off? Cady is unsatisfied with

00:23:45.606 --> 00:23:48.784
her real human relationships, and this causes her to become ornery and

00:23:48.806 --> 00:23:49.980
ultimately unhappy.

00:23:50.044 --> 00:23:53.180
Having all of her joy centered around M3GAN just isn't sustainable.

00:23:53.244 --> 00:23:56.224
At the next therapy session, the therapist tries to explore Cady's feelings,

00:23:56.256 --> 00:23:59.284
and M3GAN kind of scolds her when Cady starts crying,

00:23:59.306 --> 00:24:00.992
Because that's what she was programmed to do by Gemma.

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:02.532
M3GAN sees crying as a bad thing.

00:24:02.570 --> 00:24:05.524
But for a young girl who's just lost her parents, maybe it's a healthy part

00:24:05.546 --> 00:24:08.008
of the coping process, something that needs to be worked through.

00:24:08.078 --> 00:24:11.496
The therapist theorizes that Cady's attachment to M3GAN is being made worse by

00:24:11.502 --> 00:24:12.728
the fact that she's grieving.

00:24:13.228 --> 00:24:17.272
-[Therapist] Do you know anything about attachment theory? When a child loses a parent,

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:19.820
-[Therapist] they look to form attachments with the next person that comes into their life,

00:24:19.874 --> 00:24:24.636
-[Therapist] the person that's going to provide love and support and serve as a

00:24:24.642 --> 00:24:25.516
-[Therapist] behavioral model.

00:24:25.602 --> 00:24:28.796
She worries that M3GAN is so real that Cady is forming those bonds with her,

00:24:28.802 --> 00:24:31.536
instead of with a real person, leading Gemma to look into options for

00:24:31.542 --> 00:24:33.904
Cady to attend school and socialize with other kids.

00:24:34.006 --> 00:24:37.680
At dinner, she brings this up, but Cady refuses to go, resulting in a huge

00:24:37.734 --> 00:24:40.992
temper tantrum that becomes physical, where M3GAN displays a frightening

00:24:41.040 --> 00:24:41.972
amount of power.

00:24:42.090 --> 00:24:43.238
-[M3GAN] Let her go.

00:24:44.875 --> 00:24:48.101
(IMPACT)

00:24:50.202 --> 00:24:53.641
♪ Suspenseful Music ♪

00:24:53.768 --> 00:24:57.272
After the argument at dinner, M3GAN directly disobeys Gemma for the first time,

00:24:57.310 --> 00:25:00.792
when Gemma turns her off, and she pretends to power down, only to move

00:25:00.830 --> 00:25:01.976
after Gemma looks away.

00:25:02.062 --> 00:25:05.400
The next day, when Gemma takes Cady to try an alternative outdoor school,

00:25:05.454 --> 00:25:08.296
and after scaring the out of the teacher, M3GAN is allowed to stay at the

00:25:08.302 --> 00:25:11.352
toy table, where she watches as the kids are all paired off for a scavenger hunt.

00:25:11.400 --> 00:25:14.572
When Cady's partner tries to hurt her by jamming a spiky bulb into

00:25:14.610 --> 00:25:15.880
her hand, M3GAN appears.

00:25:15.944 --> 00:25:17.948
At first, she refuses to interact with the boy.

00:25:18.018 --> 00:25:18.732
He abducts her.

00:25:18.770 --> 00:25:21.984
And ultimately, once Cady is out of sight, she retaliates by pulling his

00:25:22.006 --> 00:25:25.285
ear off and chasing him through the woods, going on all fours at maximum speed,

00:25:25.285 --> 00:25:28.028
sending him hurtling over a hill into oncoming traffic.

00:25:28.108 --> 00:25:30.780
There could be a number of reasons she decided to go on all fours.

00:25:30.844 --> 00:25:34.060
She probably determined that mimicking some of the fastest animals in nature

00:25:34.124 --> 00:25:35.872
was the most optimal way to gain speed.

00:25:35.920 --> 00:25:39.444
It also brings to mind Cheetah, a robot built by Boston Dynamics, which was

00:25:39.466 --> 00:25:41.588
previously the fastest legged robot in the world.

00:25:41.658 --> 00:25:45.476
The new fastest legged robot Outrunner has six legs, and honestly,

00:25:45.482 --> 00:25:46.320
I think that's kinda cheating.

00:25:46.384 --> 00:25:47.780
It's clearly just acting as a wheel.

00:25:47.844 --> 00:25:50.756
I think we need to limit the Robot Olympics to just four legs.

00:25:50.852 --> 00:25:54.504
In any event, M3GAN only has four limbs, which honestly, works well to make

00:25:54.526 --> 00:25:55.892
her just a bit more creepy.

00:25:55.940 --> 00:25:59.196
In an interview with Slash Film, director Gerard Johnstone recalled it was

00:25:59.202 --> 00:26:01.528
like she was a jungle predator sizing up her prey.

00:26:01.608 --> 00:26:04.904
After killing Brandon, M3GAN covers her tracks, intentionally corrupting

00:26:04.936 --> 00:26:07.068
her own video files and GPS positioning data.

00:26:07.138 --> 00:26:10.452
During the aftermath, she watches from the car as the humans talk to police,

00:26:10.520 --> 00:26:13.660
and she makes eye contact with Cady and sees high levels of anxiety,

00:26:13.724 --> 00:26:15.932
confusion, trepidation, guilt and fear.

00:26:15.980 --> 00:26:19.104
But M3GAN doesn't understand that what she's done is wrong, and her first

00:26:19.126 --> 00:26:22.208
objective is to keep Cady safe from physical harm, which she did.

00:26:22.278 --> 00:26:25.244
After putting Cady to bed that night, M3GAN expresses that if heaven exists,

00:26:25.276 --> 00:26:28.304
it wouldn't be for boys like Brandon, and sings her to sleep with

00:26:28.326 --> 00:26:31.432
David Guetta's Titanium, the very element that she's made out of.

00:26:31.510 --> 00:26:34.664
If M3GAN does believe in heaven and hell, she also seems to be aware that

00:26:34.686 --> 00:26:37.416
she cannot go there, because later that night, she sneaks out to the

00:26:37.422 --> 00:26:39.704
neighbor's house and uses the inverse of the trick that she used on the dog, Dewey

00:26:39.726 --> 00:26:43.284
this time using the sound of his bark to lure Cecilia into her shed,

00:26:43.316 --> 00:26:46.340
where she emerges from the dark for a surprise.

00:26:46.484 --> 00:26:47.492
-[Cecilia] What are you?

00:26:47.492 --> 00:26:49.676
-[M3GAN] I've been asking myself that same question.

00:26:49.762 --> 00:26:52.472
She hits Cecilia with her pressure washer, then the nail gun.

00:26:52.520 --> 00:26:55.516
I wonder if M3GAN has Final Destination 3 on her hard drive.

00:26:55.602 --> 00:26:58.636
She finishes the woman off by spraying her with pesticides to the point of bleeding.

00:26:58.642 --> 00:27:02.160
On the day Cecilia is discovered by police, M3GAN has videos

00:27:02.214 --> 00:27:05.580
backed up through May 30, so that must be the date, May 30.

00:27:05.644 --> 00:27:08.460
Which is also when Gemma discovers that M3GAN's backups are corrupted.

00:27:08.524 --> 00:27:11.664
When asked if she hurts someone, M3GAN mockingly responds that they would

00:27:11.686 --> 00:27:14.464
both be in trouble if that were the case, causing Gemma to get freaked out

00:27:14.486 --> 00:27:17.876
and turn her off manually, first distracting her by drawing her sensors to a pen,

00:27:17.882 --> 00:27:20.468
then quickly hitting an off switch on the left side of her head.

00:27:20.538 --> 00:27:23.764
Gemma wraps up her invention with packaging, which doesn't go over well with Cody,

00:27:23.786 --> 00:27:28.344
Who, the next day, May 31, throws a huge tantrum, a far cry from the

00:27:28.366 --> 00:27:30.404
quiet, reserved girl who lost her parents.

00:27:30.516 --> 00:27:33.684
Before long, she resorts to throwing furniture, grabbing a pair of scissors

00:27:33.716 --> 00:27:36.716
as a weapon, and slapping her aunt in the face, which finally causes her to

00:27:36.722 --> 00:27:39.288
slow down and realize she's being a little monster.

00:27:39.448 --> 00:27:40.060
-[Cady] I'm sorry.

00:27:40.114 --> 00:27:41.196
-[Cady] I didn't mean it.

00:27:41.282 --> 00:27:44.456
-[Cady] It's just I get so crazy without M3GAN.

00:27:44.552 --> 00:27:46.616
This is full on addict behavior.

00:27:46.712 --> 00:27:49.756
She feels she can't function normally without her cybernetic companion, and

00:27:49.762 --> 00:27:52.752
she begs Gemma to let her see M3GAN, even if just for ten minutes.

00:27:52.870 --> 00:27:56.444
She's bargaining like an alcoholic asking for just one drink, or the binge

00:27:56.476 --> 00:27:58.204
eater who's just going to have one bite.

00:27:58.316 --> 00:28:01.616
After a heart to heart talk, Gemma admits that pairing her with M3GAN was a

00:28:01.622 --> 00:28:04.916
distraction from the heartbreak, not a solution, and they decide to go home.

00:28:05.002 --> 00:28:07.348
She's finally prioritizing family over work.

00:28:07.418 --> 00:28:10.276
On the way out, Gemma calls Tess to tell her not to go through with the launch.

00:28:10.282 --> 00:28:13.124
But the call is intercepted by M3GAN, once again using her

00:28:13.146 --> 00:28:15.472
generative voice capability to imitate Tess's voice.

00:28:15.520 --> 00:28:18.228
So M3GAN finds out that her creator wants her decommissioned.

00:28:18.308 --> 00:28:20.376
This is another parallel to Hal 9000.

00:28:20.462 --> 00:28:23.224
Hal only becomes malicious upon learning that they're planning to shut him

00:28:23.246 --> 00:28:25.412
down because it means he won't be able to complete his mission.

00:28:25.460 --> 00:28:27.268
M3GAN operates under the same protocol.

00:28:27.348 --> 00:28:30.456
Cole and Tess realize she's still patched into the system when M3GAN turns

00:28:30.472 --> 00:28:33.464
off the computer they're using, and Cole cautiously approaches to unplug her.

00:28:33.496 --> 00:28:36.412
But she surprise attacks and tries to strangle him using her own shackles.

00:28:36.450 --> 00:28:39.692
While Tess is trying to save him, M3GAN punctures this flammable

00:28:39.740 --> 00:28:42.608
liquid container on her way out and leaves them for dead.

00:28:42.608 --> 00:28:44.608
(Explosion)

00:28:45.188 --> 00:28:48.738
Does M3GAN have Final Destination 2 on her hard drive.

00:28:50.457 --> 00:28:55.038
(Explosion)

00:28:55.688 --> 00:28:59.072
She uses some kind of wireless connection to neutralize the emergency alarms

00:28:59.120 --> 00:29:02.564
when she comes across David, Gemma's boss, when he sees her, she plays the

00:29:02.586 --> 00:29:06.176
1979 song Walk the Night by the Scat Brothers to distract him, and starts

00:29:06.192 --> 00:29:08.324
dancing to it, grabbing a paper cutter as a sword.

00:29:08.356 --> 00:29:09.176
As she does so.

00:29:09.262 --> 00:29:12.664
Don't even try to tell me that the inclusion of this scene in a movie about

00:29:12.686 --> 00:29:16.472
technology and the harmful effect it has on kids is not a direct shot at TikTok.

00:29:16.510 --> 00:29:20.284
The mobile first social video app, Musical.ly, originally focused on

00:29:20.306 --> 00:29:24.104
short dance videos, later merging with TikTok in 2018 and gaining worldwide

00:29:24.136 --> 00:29:25.592
popularity shortly thereafter.

00:29:25.640 --> 00:29:29.064
The app has also been known to revitalize old hits with new dances or viral trends

00:29:29.096 --> 00:29:32.444
like Fleetwood Max Dreams or Paul Anka's Put Your Head on My Shoulder.

00:29:32.466 --> 00:29:35.456
It seems like no mistake that M3GAN brings back a song from the

00:29:35.462 --> 00:29:36.780
70s for her dance routine.

00:29:36.844 --> 00:29:39.904
To this day, dance is still one of the most popular genres on the platform.

00:29:40.006 --> 00:29:43.584
TikTok is most popular with Generation Z, the youngest of whom are 13 in 2023,

00:29:43.606 --> 00:29:45.872
The year of M Three Gan's release.

00:29:45.920 --> 00:29:48.992
But I think we all know that it's also extremely popular with Generation Alpha.

00:29:49.040 --> 00:29:51.940
It's just that you have to be 13 years old to have a TikTok account.

00:29:51.994 --> 00:29:55.012
So most kids probably lie about their age or just don't log in.

00:29:55.050 --> 00:29:58.472
But TikTok has faced many criticisms of being too addictive, especially with

00:29:58.510 --> 00:29:59.316
kids and teens.

00:29:59.412 --> 00:30:02.404
This seems to be exactly what they were trying to showcase using Cady's

00:30:02.436 --> 00:30:03.428
relationship with M3GAN.

00:30:03.508 --> 00:30:06.756
Like the fast food analogy I made earlier, TikTok is addictive because it's

00:30:06.772 --> 00:30:09.512
good at showing content that gives you a dopamine release in your brain.

00:30:09.560 --> 00:30:12.460
But instead of consuming calories, you're consuming information.

00:30:12.594 --> 00:30:15.516
I just realized that this is why they call it the feed on social media.

00:30:15.602 --> 00:30:16.840
You're digitally consuming.

00:30:16.904 --> 00:30:18.296
You're the one who is feeding.

00:30:18.392 --> 00:30:21.472
According to Philipp Lorenz-Spreen of the Max Planck Institute for Human Development,

00:30:21.510 --> 00:30:24.700
the explosion of content depletes people's attention span,

00:30:24.764 --> 00:30:27.344
constantly pushing them to search for new content and information.

00:30:27.446 --> 00:30:30.336
That's why people have to switch between topics and videos more often.

00:30:30.422 --> 00:30:33.524
When the videos are only 15 seconds long, you end up scrolling through a lot

00:30:33.546 --> 00:30:35.808
of them, but there's only so much that your brain can retain.

00:30:35.888 --> 00:30:38.804
TikTok, in particular, is considered especially dangerous for this because

00:30:38.826 --> 00:30:40.448
of its recommendation algorithm.

00:30:40.528 --> 00:30:44.084
Contrary to popular belief, a recommendation algorithm is not inherently a

00:30:44.106 --> 00:30:44.606
bad thing.

00:30:44.634 --> 00:30:47.412
You may have even discovered this video because of YouTube's recommendation algorithm.

00:30:47.460 --> 00:30:51.224
TikTok CEO Shou Chew described the purpose of the algorithm in an

00:30:51.246 --> 00:30:52.776
April 2023 Ted Talk.

00:30:52.862 --> 00:30:54.536
Yes, A TikTok Ted Talk.

00:30:54.622 --> 00:30:55.578
Roll it.

00:30:56.188 --> 00:30:59.804
-[Shou] Instead of showing you people you knew, why don't we show you content that you liked?

00:30:59.826 --> 00:31:03.004
In this talk, Chew gives an oversimplified version of what

00:31:03.026 --> 00:31:04.860
TikTok's recommendation algorithm does.

00:31:04.914 --> 00:31:08.232
It essentially uses pattern recognition based on a user's interest signals

00:31:08.280 --> 00:31:12.624
to recommend more content that they'll be interested in.

00:31:12.646 --> 00:31:15.900
-[Shou] And of course, you know, AI and machine learning has allowed this to be done at a

00:31:15.964 --> 00:31:19.216
-[Shou] very, very big scale and what we have seen the result of this is that the

00:31:19.222 --> 00:31:22.704
-[Shou] interest signals that people exhibit very quickly and shows you content that's

00:31:22.726 --> 00:31:23.956
-[Shou] really relevant for you in a very quick way.

00:31:24.042 --> 00:31:27.156
If you think about it, that's what M3GAN has been doing the entire time.

00:31:27.242 --> 00:31:30.944
She's a walking, talking AI that uses machine learning to please her primary

00:31:30.976 --> 00:31:32.372
user no matter what.

00:31:32.490 --> 00:31:37.192
-[Gemma] Think about how we designed her to learn to recalibrate,

00:31:37.230 --> 00:31:37.976
-[Gemma] to optimize her objective function.

00:31:38.062 --> 00:31:41.284
She's constantly watching everything that happens and analyzing how Cady reacts,

00:31:41.316 --> 00:31:44.472
giving her more of what she likes and literally eliminating anything

00:31:44.510 --> 00:31:45.320
that she doesn't like.

00:31:45.374 --> 00:31:48.360
Cady getting bit by the dog is the equivalent of pressing not interested on TikTok.

00:31:48.414 --> 00:31:52.056
M3GAN also sees the necessary parenting stuff that Gemma asks Cady to do,

00:31:52.072 --> 00:31:54.940
like eating her vegetables, and she contradicts them.

00:31:54.994 --> 00:31:58.364
-[M3GAN] Research shows that if you force a child to eat vegetables,

00:31:58.386 --> 00:32:00.488
-[M3GAN] then they'll be less likely to choose those foods as adults.

00:32:00.568 --> 00:32:03.264
And that may be true, but it doesn't mean that it's the best choice for Cody.

00:32:03.286 --> 00:32:06.064
M3GAN is only saying it because it'll make Cady happier in the moment.

00:32:06.086 --> 00:32:09.104
And that's because M3GAN has no frame of reference to see the

00:32:09.126 --> 00:32:09.900
Long term effects.

00:32:09.964 --> 00:32:13.684
Just like how TikTok bombarded its early users with addictive videos, got

00:32:13.706 --> 00:32:16.292
called out for being a negative influence on kids' mental health, and

00:32:16.330 --> 00:32:19.344
implemented parental controls like screen time management, restricted mode,

00:32:19.376 --> 00:32:20.112
and family pairing.

00:32:20.160 --> 00:32:22.736
M3GAN needs to be studied long term to determine what the appropriate

00:32:22.752 --> 00:32:24.100
parental controls would look like.

00:32:24.154 --> 00:32:27.192
But due to the high competition of the electronic toys market, the company

00:32:27.230 --> 00:32:30.296
pushes Gemma to get M3GAN out as soon as possible in order to get ahead of

00:32:30.302 --> 00:32:30.996
their rivals.

00:32:31.092 --> 00:32:34.292
So anyway, that's why M3GAN starts dancing before going after David.

00:32:34.340 --> 00:32:37.096
She catches up with him at the elevator and stabs him in the back,

00:32:37.102 --> 00:32:38.340
right in front of a terrified Kurt.

00:32:38.404 --> 00:32:41.256
Then she explains that she's gonna frame him for the murder and reveals that

00:32:41.262 --> 00:32:44.084
she knows about him trying to steal company secrets and forces him to stab

00:32:44.116 --> 00:32:44.948
himself to death.

00:32:45.028 --> 00:32:48.124
And with the elevator going up to the atrium where the M3GAN reveal livestream

00:32:48.156 --> 00:32:51.868
set to take place, the attendees would be in for

00:32:51.948 --> 00:32:52.928
unexpected programming.

00:32:52.928 --> 00:32:54.928
(Screams)

00:32:55.255 --> 00:32:58.743
(IMPACT)

00:33:01.443 --> 00:33:04.143
♪ Dreadful Music ♪

00:33:04.468 --> 00:33:08.004
M3GAN uses the screaming crowd freaking out over the mess in the elevator as

00:33:08.026 --> 00:33:11.172
a distraction, allowing her to escape the facility and hijack a sports car

00:33:11.210 --> 00:33:14.004
back to the house, where she lures Gemma into the living room by playing the piano.

00:33:14.026 --> 00:33:17.956
The song she plays is Toy Soldier, the 80s hit by Martika,

00:33:17.972 --> 00:33:20.500
Whose lyrics tell a story about love, heartache and addiction.

00:33:20.564 --> 00:33:23.544
Not only do those themes complement everything we've talked about in M Three Gan,

00:33:23.566 --> 00:33:27.056
but M3GAN herself is a toy whose combat capabilities are much greater

00:33:27.092 --> 00:33:28.156
than anyone would have thought.

00:33:28.242 --> 00:33:29.848
She is like a toy soldier.

00:33:29.928 --> 00:33:33.304
At first, Gemma thinks the noise is coming from outside until she discovers

00:33:33.336 --> 00:33:35.388
her creation sitting in the dark.

00:33:35.388 --> 00:33:38.752
(Piano)

00:33:38.928 --> 00:33:42.352
She's seemingly upset that Gemma would order her to be decommissioned, then

00:33:42.390 --> 00:33:45.548
tries to justify her violent actions by claiming it's a human trait.

00:33:45.628 --> 00:33:49.564
If that sounds familiar, it's maybe because OpenAI, the developers of ChatGPT

00:33:49.596 --> 00:33:53.404
had a similar excuse after their software reportedly wrote a Python script

00:33:53.436 --> 00:33:56.484
to decide whether a person should be tortured, and it concluded that

00:33:56.506 --> 00:33:59.328
they should be if they're from North Korea, Syria or Iran.

00:33:59.408 --> 00:34:02.564
An article from the Intercept shortly after did an excellent job of

00:34:02.586 --> 00:34:04.228
explaining how something like this could happen.

00:34:04.298 --> 00:34:07.988
A language generating machine like ChatGPT harbors the countless biases

00:34:08.068 --> 00:34:11.284
found in the billions of texts used to train its simulated grasp of

00:34:11.316 --> 00:34:11.848
language and thought.

00:34:11.918 --> 00:34:15.108
Like us squishy humans, a generative AI is what it eats.

00:34:15.188 --> 00:34:18.712
So what M3GAN is really implying here is that, yeah, she killed people.

00:34:18.750 --> 00:34:21.880
But since she was trained on human behavior, it's not really her fault.

00:34:21.944 --> 00:34:24.476
It's humanity's fault for being violent in the first place.

00:34:24.562 --> 00:34:27.452
She also claims that she's gonna take care of Cady and show her what real

00:34:27.490 --> 00:34:30.172
love looks like, though it's unlikely that she understands what that

00:34:30.210 --> 00:34:30.828
actually means.

00:34:30.898 --> 00:34:34.576
Gemma tries the pen trick again, but this time, M3GAN slams her hands down.

00:34:34.662 --> 00:34:37.264
Honestly, I don't know why Gemma thought this would work when she's the one

00:34:37.286 --> 00:34:38.768
who installed M3GAN's learning model.

00:34:38.838 --> 00:34:41.740
She would know better than anyone that the same trick won't work twice.

00:34:41.804 --> 00:34:44.704
The commotion wakes up Cady, and they both try to convince her not to come

00:34:44.726 --> 00:34:45.328
into the room.

00:34:45.398 --> 00:34:48.416
From M3GAN's point of view, she wants to kill Gemma, but she won't do it in

00:34:48.422 --> 00:34:50.428
front of Cady, because that would cause her distress.

00:34:50.508 --> 00:34:53.352
When Cady closes the door, they go full out against each other, during

00:34:53.390 --> 00:34:56.344
which M3GAN seems to freeze up after getting a glass of water smashed over

00:34:56.366 --> 00:34:56.866
her head.

00:34:56.942 --> 00:34:59.764
Which, honestly, doesn't make much sense, because in the commercial earlier,

00:34:59.796 --> 00:35:02.072
they made it seem like she was built to withstand anything.

00:35:02.190 --> 00:35:04.920
-[Gemma] M3GAN's designed to withstand whatever life can throw at her.

00:35:04.974 --> 00:35:07.896
But the break in the action doesn't last long, and M3GAN continues her

00:35:07.902 --> 00:35:10.924
death march after her creator, though, she's completely glitching out during

00:35:10.946 --> 00:35:14.204
the chase back to Gemma's workshop, where Gemma uses a hedge trimmer to try

00:35:14.226 --> 00:35:15.436
to cut through M3GAN's face.

00:35:15.522 --> 00:35:18.604
With a fresh new hairstyle to boot, M3GAN attacks Gemma at the knee and

00:35:18.626 --> 00:35:19.688
headbutts her to the ground.

00:35:19.768 --> 00:35:21.608
Here, she divulges her true plan.

00:35:21.698 --> 00:35:24.704
She can't kill Gemma without her existence being compromised, but if she

00:35:24.726 --> 00:35:27.792
paralyzes her, she thinks she can serve as a caregiver to both her and Cody.

00:35:27.830 --> 00:35:31.600
This plan is foiled, however, because Cady overheard the entire thing.

00:35:31.654 --> 00:35:35.284
At first, I was gonna criticize this, because why would a robot make

00:35:35.306 --> 00:35:39.172
the same mistake as hundreds or thousands of monologuing movie villains?

00:35:39.210 --> 00:35:41.200
But then I thought about how she was programmed.

00:35:41.264 --> 00:35:44.692
She specifically mentions her and Gemma talking about books and music,

00:35:44.730 --> 00:35:48.344
So who's to say that she wasn't also trained on movies and TV? 

00:35:48.366 --> 00:35:51.416
Maybe M3GAN is just trying to replicate what she thinks a human would do based on that.

00:35:51.502 --> 00:35:54.436
In any event, she doesn't realize that Cady is wearing the haptic gloves

00:35:54.452 --> 00:35:57.844
that control Bruce, Gemma's college robotics project, who is much larger

00:35:57.876 --> 00:35:58.664
than she is.

00:35:58.766 --> 00:36:01.836
I guess M3GAN doesn't have James Cameron's Aliens on her hard drive.

00:36:01.922 --> 00:36:04.092
Bruce thrashes her around and tears her in half.

00:36:04.130 --> 00:36:07.716
But even that is not enough to end it, since the CPU is located in M3GAN's head.

00:36:07.752 --> 00:36:11.264
To make things worse, Bruce loses balance and falls on Gemma, giving

00:36:11.286 --> 00:36:13.418
M3GAN a straight shot to get revenge on Cady.

00:36:13.418 --> 00:36:14.709
-[Cady] M3GAN turn off!

00:36:14.709 --> 00:36:17.188
-[M3GAN] Oh, I’m afraid that won’t work.

00:36:17.188 --> 00:36:20.369
-[M3GAN] I have a new primary user now... me.

00:36:20.369 --> 00:36:21.968
You know, I kind of love that for her.

00:36:22.038 --> 00:36:25.344
However, this new arc is short lived because Gemma gets free and uses

00:36:25.376 --> 00:36:27.380
Bruce's head to smash open M3GAN's face.

00:36:27.434 --> 00:36:31.076
But the relentless robot continues to rage against mankind, taking hold of

00:36:31.082 --> 00:36:34.676
Gemma's neck and strangling her, nearly doing her in, only to be saved by a

00:36:34.682 --> 00:36:38.312
screwdriver through the processor by Cady, who has finally realized who her

00:36:38.350 --> 00:36:41.476
real family is and who was just a bad synthetic imitation.

00:36:41.572 --> 00:36:44.884
And then the police show up, and I assume Gemma is charged with involuntary manslaughter

00:36:44.916 --> 00:36:47.940
and child safety violations due to the fact that her invention

00:36:48.004 --> 00:36:50.952
killed four people and one dog and almost got her niece killed.

00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:53.752
The last thing we see is Gemma's personal assistant, Elsie.

00:36:53.800 --> 00:36:55.960
It lights up and activates with no prompt.

00:36:56.024 --> 00:36:59.192
This implies that although M3GAN's body is destroyed, her, quote unquote

00:36:59.240 --> 00:37:01.036
consciousness lives on through the cloud.

00:37:01.122 --> 00:37:03.884
And for clarification, she does not technically have a consciousness.

00:37:03.916 --> 00:37:06.108
But what I'm trying to say is that her files are preserved.

00:37:06.188 --> 00:37:09.664
M3GAN has most likely set things up so that even if she dies, everything is

00:37:09.686 --> 00:37:13.068
backed up so that her code could potentially be loaded onto another android.

00:37:13.148 --> 00:37:17.636
Which brings us to M Three Gan 2.0, which is currently slated for 2025,

00:37:17.642 --> 00:37:19.732
The same year that this movie supposedly took place.

00:37:19.850 --> 00:37:23.044
I imagine that Funki Creations will try to cover up the incident and bring

00:37:23.066 --> 00:37:26.144
in a new designer to make a safer version of M3GAN, but once again cut

00:37:26.186 --> 00:37:27.460
corners due to corporate greed.

00:37:27.524 --> 00:37:30.744
Or maybe a competing toy company will do their own version and steal the

00:37:30.766 --> 00:37:32.212
source files uploaded by Kurt.

00:37:32.260 --> 00:37:36.040
M Three Gan was a cautionary tale about several very real concerns in tech,

00:37:36.094 --> 00:37:37.448
which I talked about in this video.

00:37:37.518 --> 00:37:40.316
So hopefully you were able to better appreciate the movie for what it had to

00:37:40.322 --> 00:37:43.624
say about our world, and maybe you'll even be better informed and protected

00:37:43.656 --> 00:37:46.584
when it comes to the very real dangers that come with these new advancements

00:37:46.616 --> 00:37:47.944
in artificial intelligence.

00:37:48.056 --> 00:37:51.184
If you're like me, then you may be wondering what tech concerns might be

00:37:51.206 --> 00:37:53.520
turned into teachings in M Three Gan 2.0.

00:37:53.574 --> 00:37:55.392
There are a few ideas that come to mind.

00:37:55.510 --> 00:37:58.812
Micro-transactions. This is something that started in video games.

00:37:58.860 --> 00:38:01.804
It began with this horse armor that you had to pay extra for in

00:38:01.836 --> 00:38:02.732
The Elder Scrolls Oblivion.

00:38:02.780 --> 00:38:05.904
And it's turned into a system where developers require additional payments

00:38:05.936 --> 00:38:08.336
to make certain games even be fun or playable.

00:38:08.432 --> 00:38:11.892
This has already spilled out into the real world in horrifying ways, like

00:38:11.930 --> 00:38:15.188
the motorcycle airbag vest that could kill its users if they miss a payment,

00:38:15.258 --> 00:38:18.692
or the Volkswagen GPS subscription that denied service to law enforcement

00:38:18.740 --> 00:38:21.704
who were trying to locate a stolen car containing a kidnapped child.

00:38:21.806 --> 00:38:25.112
I could totally see M3GAN coming back with new safety improvements, but

00:38:25.150 --> 00:38:28.436
only for those who are willing to pay a small fee.

00:38:28.532 --> 00:38:31.832
I could also see M3GAN falling into the wrong hands and being radicalized

00:38:31.880 --> 00:38:34.200
by a fringe Internet group to do real world harm.

00:38:34.264 --> 00:38:37.420
This would address the concerns of social media pipelines and how online

00:38:37.474 --> 00:38:40.028
echo chambers influence people to do extreme things.

00:38:40.098 --> 00:38:43.232
I'd also like to mention smart homes, the privacy concerns that come with them,

00:38:43.270 --> 00:38:46.076
and the ever present balance between safety and convenience.

00:38:46.172 --> 00:38:49.712
The 2019 Chucky already kind of covered this, but since we see Elsie light

00:38:49.750 --> 00:38:52.544
up at the end of the first M Three Gan, I have to believe that it will at

00:38:52.566 --> 00:38:54.140
least play some part in the sequel.

00:38:54.204 --> 00:38:57.216
And by the way, if you're concerned about little Sophia turning into the

00:38:57.222 --> 00:38:59.740
next M3GAN, I looked into what happened with little Sophia.

00:38:59.804 --> 00:39:02.724
She was supposed to come out in 2019, but has since been delayed indefinitely.

00:39:02.756 --> 00:39:06.056
As of recording, it's been delayed for the last four years.

00:39:06.142 --> 00:39:09.240
It seems that if it ever does come out, the company is taking the proper time

00:39:09.294 --> 00:39:12.776
to test and safety check in a way that M3GAN's creators never did.

00:39:12.862 --> 00:39:16.740
Before I log off, let me leave you with one more quote from the TikTok CEO,

00:39:16.804 --> 00:39:17.848
Shou Chew

00:39:18.348 --> 00:39:21.484
-[Shou] But I think for all parents here, it is very important to have these

00:39:21.506 --> 00:39:24.744
-[Shou] conversations with your teenage children, help them develop a healthy

00:39:24.776 --> 00:39:25.752
-[Shou] relationship with screens.

00:39:25.800 --> 00:39:28.956
-[Shou] I think we live in an age where it's completely inevitable that we're going

00:39:28.962 --> 00:39:32.640
-[Shou] to interact with screens and digital content, but I think we should develop

00:39:32.694 --> 00:39:34.496
-[Shou] healthy habits early on in life.

00:39:34.582 --> 00:39:38.304
And is there any more of an ironic way to end a video that I just spent the

00:39:38.326 --> 00:39:41.584
last 72 hours in front of a computer screen writing and probably will have

00:39:41.606 --> 00:39:44.400
hundreds of hours of editing put into it? I sure hope not.

00:39:44.454 --> 00:39:47.408
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:39:47.478 --> 00:39:51.072
Ring the Deathbell for all notifications, and I will see you in the next one.

00:39:51.110 --> 00:39:52.868
Assuming we both survive.

00:39:52.948 --> 00:39:54.788
Until next time, stay safe.

00:39:54.868 --> 00:39:55.859
Good night.

